From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:04:33 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 34/34] Plutonium: common plumbing for tab features

EXO-TAB-FEATURES (docs/features/TAB_FEATURES.md, "The common shape"):
what find, zoom, printing, permissions, file pickers and downloads share,
written once.

- Requests (plutonium_tab_requests.{h,cc}): a feature asks about a tab
  with Start({kind, detail, on_answer, on_fallback}). The shell page whose
  <embed> shows the tab, else the visible shell, gets a cancelable
  "tabrequest" event; preventDefault() takes it, answerTabRequest()
  answers it. If no shell listens or takes it, or the one that took it
  reloads, closes or stops listening, the fallback runs (posted, never
  from inside Start()). Destroying the Handle cancels it; an agent's
  answer, a cancel or the tab closing sends "tabrequestend" to the taker.
- State: TabInfo::state_json, a JSON object features set with
  SetTabState(); "pending" lists the open requests by kind. It reaches
  shells (BrowserTabEntry.stateJson, tabchanged) and agents
  (Plutonium.Tab.stateJson).
- Commands: TabCommand's enum becomes a name with JSON arguments and a
  JSON result (WindowBroker.RunTabCommand, tabCommand() returning a
  promise, Plutonium.tabCommand). Features add theirs with AddCommand().
- Keys: Ctrl+F, F3, Ctrl+G, Ctrl+P, Ctrl+plus/minus/0 run the matching
  command once the page let the key through, if a feature added it.
- Agents: Plutonium.answerTabRequest; each kind decides which answers it
  takes from an agent.
- Tab::AttachHelpers(), where features attach their WebContents helpers.
- --plutonium-test-tab-requests adds a "test-request" command, which
  asks a request of kind "test" and resolves with how it ended.
